        {
          "id": 3495977022,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Unless I'm missing something, fast seek applies to reading, not writing, presumably; this file just handles writing. The reading code is in wiretap/file_wrappers.c.\n\nSo should this code not say anything about fast seeking at all?\n\n(Or is this in case we want to support files open for reading *and* writing, with random access *for reading* being in supported in the part that's already been written?)",
